{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The USB 3.0 extensions meet a concrete desk need: more reach with faster transfer support than my existing USB 2.0 extension.",
    "The memory card and reader fit my Raspberry Pi use and card transfers, provided the card format and compatibility check out."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HDMI cable, touchpad keyboard and Ethernet cables fit my activities, but I already have items serving those purposes and do not need replacements now.",
    "The optical audio cable and streaming stick assume entertainment needs I have not expressed, while the 24-port switch and large internal SSDs require projects I am not currently planning."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying electronics accessories seems to have been taken as interest in almost any computer or entertainment upgrade.",
    "My networking and storage purchases seem to have been interpreted as needing more ports or much larger drives, without a specific use for that capacity."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My existing accessories matter: another similar item becomes useful when it adds a capability or solves a remaining need, rather than repeating what I already have.",
    "My recent purchases support practical desk organization and wired connectivity; portable memory for my Raspberry Pi is a different need from replacing an internal SATA drive."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my hands-on electronics use but sometimes mistake related equipment for something I currently need."
}"}
